  "investigation_notes": "Current status: no ongoing failure proven - system looks healthy now, with one transient failure seen.\n\nEvidence:\n\n* Both containers `running` (E1), app `running` exit 0 no OOM, mount `/srv/lab-data` -> `/data` `rw:true` user `1000:1000` (E7), db `running` `healthy` user root volume for pgdata (E10).\n* App `/health` `200 {\"status\":\"ok\"}` (E2), also `GET /health 200 OK` in logs (E12).\n* DB log shows `database system is ready to accept connections` no errors (E9), events show `health_status: healthy` repeatedly, normal `start/stop/destroy/rename` from test harness, no `die` with error exit (E8).\n* Storage now has space: `/srv/lab-data` `9.0%` used `410.6 MB` available `inode 0.2%` (E4), `/` `6.8%` used `inode 1.5%` (E5).\n* Upload dirs writable by app user: `/srv/lab-data/uploads` owner `1000:1000` `0755` `app_user_can_write:true` (E6), `/srv/lab-data` same (E11).\n\nTransient symptom seen:\n\n* `POST /upload 500 Internal Server Error` at `15:52:27.33` with `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device` at `/app/main.py line 59 in upload out.write(chunk)` (E12, also E3).\n* Same log shows successes before and after: `POST /upload 200 OK` at `15:52:26.06` and `15:52:26.14` (E12), and after the 500, `POST /upload 200 OK` at `15:52:27.58` then `GET /files/... 200 OK` and `DELETE /files/... 200 OK` (E12, E3).\n\nReasoning:\n\n* App 500 is symptom, not root cause - caused by storage `ENOSPC` (E12).\n* `ENOSPC` normally means disk-full or inode-full, but current measurements rule out ongoing full: 9% and 6.8% used, inodes <2% (E4, E5).\n* Permissions ruled out as ongoing cause: writable (E6, E11) and uploads succeeded after error (E12).\n* DB dependency ruled out as ongoing cause: healthy and ready (E10, E9, E8).\n* Because the only direct evidence of exhaustion (E3/E12) is contradicted by later success on same filesystem (E12) and current free space (E4/E5), there is `insufficient_evidence` for an ongoing `disk-full/inode-full` cause. No persistent crash, permission, or DB cause is shown.\n\nConclusion: `healthy` at time of check / `insufficient_evidence` for persistent root cause. Past upload failure due to transient `No space left on device`, but currently uploads succeed, health ok, space free, permissions ok, DB healthy. Do not repair disk/permissions/DB without new evidence.\n",
